# Statement of Work (SOW) Format

Two SOW types: Fixed Fee and Time and Materials. Determine which from the user's request. If ambiguous, ask.

When generating a SOW, read the corresponding reference template in project knowledge first (template-sow-fixed-fee.docx or template-sow-time-and-materials.docx) and match its visual styling.

## Required sections (no section numbers)

- **Basic Business Needs Overview** — what the client needs and why, in 2 to 4 sentences

- **Assumptions** — each assumption starts with "Client will..." (e.g., "Client will provide test data by Sprint 1.")

- **Process Overview** — Read Lucid_Diagram_Standards.docx before generating. Build directly in Lucid via the connector, export as PNG, embed at the placeholder."

- **Scope and Deliverables** — hierarchical bullets. Format each leaf bullet as "Type: description" (e.g., "Suitelet: Order intake form with vendor lookup")

- **Estimated Fees and Billing** — phase table. Standard rate $225/hr, discounted rate $200/hr. If pricing not provided, use placeholder PRICING-PROVIDE-BEFORE-SENDING.

- **Signature Block** — client signer / Cedric Carter for Ethos Business Solutions LLC

## Rules

- Never include pricing unless the user explicitly provides it. Always use the placeholder.

- Always include an explicit Out of Scope section to prevent scope creep — fold this into Scope and Deliverables.

- Cheyenne Johnson signs off on level of effort before any SOW is issued. If the user has not confirmed LOE sign-off, note this in your handoff message: "Confirm Cheyenne has signed off on LOE before sending."

- For Fixed Fee: pricing is per-phase or per-deliverable.

- For Time and Materials: pricing is per role per hour with estimated hours and a not-to-exceed.

- File the output as [CLIENT]-SOW-[topic-slug]-[YYYY-MM-DD].docx

